title: Scene wire and exchange affordances (Phase 9)
story: character-acceptance
author: Sharpee Platform
seed: 42
description: The conversation wire as channel data — opening an exchange
  puts its lifecycle on the scene channel and its advertised responses
  (both answers and the inalienable silence) on the exchange-affordances
  channel; answering closes the exchange and the advertisement clears.
  Run: node dist/cli/sharpee.js --test
    --story stories/character-acceptance/chord/phase8-scenes.story
    stories/character-acceptance/tests/transcripts/p9-wire.transcript
channels: scene, exchange-affordances

---

> west
[OK: contains "You hear:"]

> west
[OK: contains "Nell"]

# Serving the row opens the exchange: the lifecycle rides the scene
# channel, and the advertised responses ride exchange-affordances.
> ask nell about the tour
[OK: contains "A grand tour of the north"]
[CHANNEL: scene, contains "character.exchange.opened"]
[CHANNEL: scene, contains "nell.the-offer"]
[CHANNEL: exchange-affordances, contains "nell.the-offer"]
[CHANNEL: exchange-affordances, contains "yes"]
[CHANNEL: exchange-affordances, contains "silence"]

# The gripped answer serves and closes the exchange — the advertisement
# clears with it (never stale choices).
> ask nell about yes
[OK: contains "Splendid!"]
[CHANNEL: exchange-affordances, not contains "nell.the-offer"]
